-- Audience rollups: pre-generated Users and Community statistics, maintained by deltas while
-- the bot ingests chat, so nothing (dashboards included) ever scans user_channel_activity.
--   1. record_message_stats() returns each user_channel_activity row's old/new values;
--      modules/AudienceDeltas.py turns them into deltas, which Get_Messages writes to the
--      insert-only STAGING tables (audience_delta, audience_month_delta, audience_video_delta,
--      audience_new_link, audience_top_candidate) in the same transaction as the messages --
--      no shared counter rows for the parallel workers to fight over, and exact even if a run
--      is killed.
--   2. Database.FoldAudience() moves staging into the rollups (single writer): at the start
--      of a run, after each channel and at the end of the run. Its Community part reads the
--      newly-linked users' other channels through idx_user_channel_activity_user_id.
--   3. build_audience_baseline.py rebuilds everything from scratch -- DuckDB on the bot's PC
--      does the grouping and pair counting, Postgres only streams user_channel_activity
--      once -- and --verify reports drift (0 after the 2026-11-08 baseline and test runs).
-- Bucket definitions: modules/AudienceDeltas.py (mirrored in audience_bucket_def). Scopes:
-- 'group:<branch>/<group>', 'branch:<branch>', 'company' (talent channels only) and
-- 'official'.

